{"name":"Old Vine","hex":"#687760","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"old","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Mochi."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of an object, concept, relationship, etc., having existed for a relatively long period of time.","Of a living being, having lived for most of the expected years."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/old"},{"term":"vine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any plant whose stem requires support and which climbs by tendrils or twining.","Any plant the stem of which creeps along the ground."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Old vine","blocks":[{"text":"Old vine, a common description on wine labels, indicates that a wine is the product of grape vines that are notably old. There is a general belief that older vines, when properly handled, will give a better wine. There is no legal or generally agreed definition for old."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Old_and_young_riesling_vines.jpg/330px-Old_and_young_riesling_vines.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_vine","wikidata":"Q290102"},{"title":"Vine","blocks":[{"text":"A vine is any plant with a growth habit of trailing or scandent stems, lianas, or runners. The word vine can also refer to such stems or runners themselves, for instance, when used in wicker work."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/%22A_Momordica_charantia-_bitter_guard_plant%22.jpg/330px-%22A_Momordica_charantia-_bitter_guard_plant%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vine","wikidata":"Q917284"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Maribor_Zametovka_vine_and_daughter.png/500px-Maribor_Zametovka_vine_and_daughter.pn